      },
      "text": "ROLLING SHUTTER (default CMOS):\n    Rows exposed and read sequentially (top-to-bottom)\n    Different rows captured at slightly different times\n    Exposure time: each row starts ~5–10ms after previous\n    → PROBLEM: fast-moving subjects distort (\"jello effect\" in video)\n    → Sports: moving vertical bars skew diagonally\n    → Benefits: simple; most pixels; silent (electronic only)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-DIGITAL-SENSORS.md#025",
      "path": [
        "06-DIGITAL-SENSORS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:photography:06-digital-sensors, git-history:photography:06-digital-sensors]",
        "canonical_path": "photography/06-DIGITAL-SENSORS.md",
        "concepts": "[digital, sensors]",
        "current_path": "photography/06-DIGITAL-SENSORS.md",
        "id": "maxim:photography:digital-sensors",
