        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[digital, sensors]",
        "section": "photography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Digital Sensors",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GLOBAL SHUTTER:\n    All pixels exposed simultaneously → captured at exactly same instant\n    Requires: storage node per pixel (holds charge while others read)\n    → More transistors → lower fill factor → smaller effective area → more noise\n    → Or stacked BSI design to regain fill factor\n    Nikon Z9, Sony A9 III (2024): full global shutter from stacked sensors\n    → No mechanical shutter needed; 120fps; 1/16000s max; flash sync at any speed\n```"
    },
